course: dictionary
lesson: 6602
title: Nomadic: always on the move
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some people do not stay in one home all their lives. «Nomadic» describes people who move from place to place instead of living in one fixed home.
explain: Look at the clues in this sentence: «On the steppe, dry grassland too dry for crops in many places, and in deserts many peoples lived as nomadic herders, moving with their animals to find fresh grass and water.» The words moving, fresh grass and water, and with their animals all point to travelling in search of food.
explain: Nomadic is the opposite of settled. A settled family stays in one place for years. Try the swap test: «many peoples lived as herders, moving with their animals» still makes sense without the word nomadic, so nomadic must mean moving from place to place.
fact: Nomadic means moving from place to place instead of living in one fixed home.
fact: Nomadic people often follow food, water or grass for their animals.
fact: Bedouin, Mongolian herders and some Sámi reindeer herders live nomadic ways of life.
fact: Nomadic animals wander over a large area and do not stay in one territory.
fact: Informally, a nomadic life means someone keeps moving house, school or job. The opposite of nomadic is settled.
exercise: «Many peoples lived as nomadic herders, moving with their animals.» What does nomadic mean? | Staying in one fixed home all year | Growing crops in one field | Living under the sea | *Moving from place to place
exercise: Which word means the opposite of nomadic? | roaming | travelling | *settled | wandering
exercise: Dana's family has moved house, school and job many times. Her family has a nomadic life, always moving on. What does this tell you about Dana's life? | She lives in a castle on a hill | She is always sleeping under the sea | She has never left her home town | *She is used to moving and does not stay in one home
test: «Nomadic herders moved with their animals to find fresh grass.» Why did they move? | To hide from the sun | *To find food and water for their animals | To watch television | To build a bigger castle
test: Which word describes animals that wander over a large area and do not stay in one territory? | *Nomadic | Settled | Barely | Glum
exam: Which sentence uses nomadic correctly? | The nomadic town was built on one hill | The nomadic oak tree grew in the same spot for a hundred years | *The Bedouin were a nomadic people who travelled with their herds | The nomadic lamp was bright
